How can I generate a sorted output from a JSON data without using any built-in sorting functions or libraries and without explicitly sorting the data? Specifically, given the following JSON data:
{
  "students": [
    {"name": "John", "age": 25},
    {"name": "Jane", "age": 20},
    {"name": "Bob", "age": 30},
    {"name": "Alice", "age": 22}
  ]
}
How can I output the list of students sorted by their age in ascending order, using only fundamental programming constructs?

