How can I use PHP to validate a credit card number and check which company issued it? Can you provide a sample code using Luhn algorithm and regular expressions?
Here is a sample code:
$creditCardNumber = "4111 1111 1111 1111";
$creditCardNumber = str_replace(' ', '', $creditCardNumber);
if (!preg_match("/^[0-9]{15,16}$/", $creditCardNumber)) {
    echo "Invalid credit card number";
} else {
    $sum = 0;
    $length = strlen($creditCardNumber);
    for ($i = $length - 1; $i >= 0; $i--) {
        $digit = intval($creditCardNumber[$i]);
        if ($i % 2 == $length % 2) {
            $digit *= 2;
            if ($digit > 9) {
                $digit -= 9;
            }
        }
        $sum += $digit;
    }
    if ($sum % 10 == 0) {
        if (preg_match("/^4/", $creditCardNumber)) {
            echo "Visa card";
        } else if (preg_match("/^5[1-5]/", $creditCardNumber)) {
            echo "Mastercard";
        } else if (preg_match("/^3[47]/", $creditCardNumber)) {
            echo "American Express";
        } else {
            echo "Unknown card company";
        }
    } else {
        echo "Invalid credit card number";
    }
} 
This code will remove spaces from the input, check if it is a valid credit card number using Luhn algorithm, and then use regular expressions to identify the company that issued the card.

