One example of a multifaceted issue in Go programming language could be a concurrency problem, where multiple processes are accessing shared data and causing race conditions. To solve this issue, one approach could be to use Go's built-in synchronization primitives, such as channels and mutexes, to ensure that only one process can access the shared data at a time.
